 *> Implementation test of the width limit of the sign editor (T53032; docs/protocol/40-menus-8 section 6.2 step 5 and the table of the standing and hanging sign):
*> Open Sign Editor for a standing sign limits a line to 90 font pixels (SG-MAXW), for a hanging sign (ceiling) and a wall hanging sign to 60; a position that holds
*> no sign (an unloaded cell) keeps 90.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-SIGN-EDIT-WIDTH.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-KEYSTR              PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW-TEXT            PIC X(819).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SIGN                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HANGING             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-WALL-HANGING        BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 70.
 01 WS-Z                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-SIDE-PASS           BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 256.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 0 TO PK-COUNT
     MOVE CT-TYPE-STANDARD TO CT-SET-TYPE
     CALL "CONTENT-SET-COUNTS"
     MOVE 1 TO CT-OPEN
     MOVE 384 TO PL-HEIGHT
     MOVE -64 TO PL-MIN-Y
     MOVE 1 TO PL-HAS-SKY
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     MOVE "oak_sign" TO WS-KEYSTR
     CALL "CONTENT-BLOCK-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEYSTR WS-ID WS-ROW-TEXT WS-STATUS
     CALL "CONTENT-STATE-DEFAULT" USING WS-ID WS-SIGN WS-STATUS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEYSTR
     MOVE "oak_hanging_sign" TO WS-KEYSTR
     CALL "CONTENT-BLOCK-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEYSTR WS-ID WS-ROW-TEXT WS-STATUS
     CALL "CONTENT-STATE-DEFAULT" USING WS-ID WS-HANGING WS-STATUS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEYSTR
     MOVE "oak_wall_hanging_sign" TO WS-KEYSTR
     CALL "CONTENT-BLOCK-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEYSTR WS-ID WS-ROW-TEXT WS-STATUS
     CALL "CONTENT-STATE-DEFAULT" USING WS-ID WS-WALL-HANGING WS-STATUS
     CALL "WORLD-CLEAR" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "WORLD-ROW-NEW" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ZERO WS-ZERO WS-ROW
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE

*>   A cell that holds no sign (air): the standing sign's 90.
     PERFORM OPEN-EDITOR
     MOVE "sign editor width a position with no sign keeps the limit 90" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 90 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SG-MAXW TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     CALL "WORLD-BLOCK-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-SIGN
     PERFORM OPEN-EDITOR
     MOVE "sign editor width a standing sign allows 90 pixels" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 90 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SG-MAXW TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     CALL "WORLD-BLOCK-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-HANGING
     PERFORM OPEN-EDITOR
     MOVE "sign editor width a hanging sign allows 60 pixels" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 60 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SG-MAXW TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     CALL "WORLD-BLOCK-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-WALL-HANGING
     PERFORM OPEN-EDITOR
     MOVE "sign editor width a wall hanging sign allows 60 pixels" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 60 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SG-MAXW TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.

*> Open Sign Editor (05a 0x3D) for WS-X, WS-Y, WS-Z and the front side.
 OPEN-EDITOR.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-POSITION" USING PB-BUFFER WS-X WS-Y WS-Z
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-SIDE-PASS
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "SIGN-OPEN" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER.
 END PROGRAM TEST-SIGN-EDIT-WIDTH.
 COPY CLTEST.
